<title>UK: Salomon to launch 3-yr dollar Eurobond for Sibneft.</title>
<headline>Salomon to launch 3-yr dollar Eurobond for Sibneft.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers said in a statement on Wednesday it would launch a dollar-denominated Eurobond for the Russian oil company A.O. Siberian Oil Company Sibneft.  </p>
<p>Price talk is three-month dollar LIBOR plus 400 basis points area.</p>
<p>The official launch and pricing is expected on Friday.  </p>
<p>The expected settlement date is August 15, 1997. There will be Russian Federation and U.S. sales restrictions.</p>
<p>English law applies and the bonds will be listed on the Luxembourg stock exchange.</p>
<p>The issue is unrated.</p>
<p>It is the first Russian corporate issuer to publicly access the international debt capital markets, Salomon Brothers said.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
